# Local tooling, not the site.
.claude/

# Secrets live in Vercel's environment (KV_REST_API_TOKEN, BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN,
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, KNOLL_OWNER_KEY…), never in a file here — and a .env
# made for a local run must never reach git or the deploy (.vercelignore too).
.env
.env.*

# lab 2's performance workbench keeps its evidence here: ~53MB of screen
# captures, traces and run logs across 148 PNGs and 20 logs. The harnesses
# that produce them are worth keeping and are tracked; the output of a run
# that has already been read is not. Held off the deploy separately by
# .vercelignore, which excludes the whole of lab2/perf — git has no
# .vercelignore to read, so the two lists differ on purpose.
lab2/perf/results/

# The shortcuts and scratch files that live beside lab 2 on this machine.
lab2/index.html.keep-bak
lab2/*.tmp
lab2/*.bat
lab2/*.ico
lab2/*.lnk

# And the same beside the iron hive, which has its own one-click starter and
# its own autosave door — the page and its stickers are the site, the .bat and
# the .lnk that open them are this machine.
ironhive/*.keep-bak
ironhive/*.tmp
ironhive/*.bat
ironhive/*.ico
ironhive/*.lnk

# The hive keeps its probes at its own root rather than in a perf/ of its own,
# so their screenshots land beside the page. Same rule as lab2/perf/results:
# the harness is worth keeping, the output of a run already read is not — and
# no PNG here is part of the site (the favicon is the .ico above).
ironhive/*.png
ironhive/results/

# TOEM 2 is a third bench of the same kind (lab 2 with the paper cleared, and
# its own sticker drawer and wall seed), so the same rules again beside it.
# (*.keep-bak: serve.js backs up index.html and, since TOEM 2's save button,
# wall-seed.json too, once a run.)
toem2/*.keep-bak
toem2/*.tmp
toem2/*.bat
toem2/*.ico
toem2/*.lnk
toem2/*.png
toem2/results/
# …and the wall's editing door (api/wall.js) keeps everything — the wall,
# the queue, who is who — in this file when it runs off Vercel with no
# Redis; wall-seed.json beside it is the copy that ships.
toem2/wall-db.json
toem2/wall-db.json.tmp
# …and the sign-up codes the dev server's stand-in postman writes beside it (api/auth.js: THE POSTMAN)
toem2/outbox.jsonl
# …and the photo album's pictures (api/gallery.js) land beside it, off Vercel
toem2/album/

# Benches made by lab 2's "+ new bench" (serve.js, from lab2/bench-template):
# each bench is the site; its backups and a folder left half-made are this
# machine's.
folder_*/*.keep-bak
folder_*/*.tmp
.folder_*.making/

# The yard's publish door (api/hill.js, mounted by serve.js) keeps every local
# save as a version here; yard/hill.json beside it is the one that ships.
yard/looks/

# The one-click starter beside the yard, and its two shortcuts (Yard.lnk here,
# Yard View.lnk in YardView/, both running yard/start-yard.bat) with their icons:
# this machine, the way the benches' own .bat, .lnk and .ico are.
yard/*.bat
yard/*.lnk
yard/*.ico
YardView/*.lnk
YardView/*.ico
